addition, the company offers corporate and individual trust and agency, investment management, and real estate investment trust services; debit and credit cards; treasury management; and remote deposit, merchant processing, online payment portal, lockbox, smart safe, ACH origination, online bill pay, wire transfer, and positive and reverse positive pay services, as well as sells various life insurance products. Further, it provides online and mobile banking; health savings accounts; wealth management, financial planning, investment management, and insurance services; retirement services, including individual retirement accounts (IRAs), business IRAs, and employee benefit plans; and estate planning and settlement services. Horizon Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1873 and is headquartered in Michigan City, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas M. Prame | CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 465 people. Each employee generates $160K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Horizon Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.1B market cap on $27M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $74M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 6.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fun